  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$10$ per meter (dollars per meter). To find how many meters of rope she can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in meters per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n10\\,\\text{dollars per meter}\\,\\to \\,1÷10=0.1\\,\\text{meters per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.1$ meters per dollar. Therefore, Maya can buy $0.1$ meters of rope for $1$ dollar.",
